cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Logos-Formal: Fail-Closed Separation of AI Interpretation from Authorization"
authors:
  - family-names: "McClure II"
    given-names: "Charles LeRoy"
repository-code: "https://github.com/XRastlinX/logos-formal"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-26"
abstract: >-
  A formal governance architecture that enforces fail-closed separation
  between AI interpretation (planning, observation, estimation) and
  authorization (human permission, systemic actuation). Implements the
  PIC-4 (Pure Invariant Constructor) model, aligning agentic AI control
  with IETF RATS (RFC 9334) and NIST ABAC (SP 800-162) standards.
  Includes runnable Go demonstrators for permit-gated actuation,
  cross-field epistemic translation, and autophagic decay simulation.
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - formal-methods
  - capability-separation
  - attestation
  - remote-attestation
  - access-control
  - fail-closed
  - governance
  - supply-chain-security
  - zero-trust
